    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner return `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names. Two changes accomplish this:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gains a `displayName` field (with getter/setter).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the field from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\n`GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns e.g. `\"Franklin, George\"`. The full suite passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` asserting `$.displayName == \"<lastName>, John\"`.",
